  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly continues a comma after the opening time phrase with a proper name, but the representative prefix has no earlier person for the existing capture-based Lily rule to reuse; the prediction instead puts nearly all its mass on <END>. Add a general comma-suffix rule to each declared proper-name output so the name remains uncertain rather than forcing Lily. The batch also repeatedly targets day after a determiner and adjective (for example, “a sunny”), which the existing day rule matching only a final determiner misses. These repairs generalize over names and adjectives and do not assert that every comma or adjective must have these continuations; other valid continuations remain available. The replay gate has not evaluated this proposal.",
